Package: ls.dynam
Type: Package
Title: Latent Space Dynamic Network Actor Models with a Position-Rate Link
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alberto", "Caimo", email = "alberto.caimo@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8956-7166")),
    person("Isabella", "Gollini", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7738-5688")))
Description: Bayesian inference for latent space dynamic network actor models
    of relational event data. An actor's activity follows a Poisson-type rate
    model with random activity effects, and its choice of receivers follows a
    conditional logit model with latent sender and receiver positions. A
    position-rate link relates summaries of the positions that the choice
    model identifies, such as latent popularity and excess self-affinity, to
    the activity effects through a spline regression. Inference is modular:
    the positions are estimated from the choice of receivers alone, by a
    Metropolis-adjusted Langevin algorithm (MALA) or a Laplace approximation, and the
    link is estimated under the plug-in or the cut posterior. The package also
    provides Bayes factors for the link and its components, held-out
    predictive scores, calibration by simulation, diagnostics and a simulator.
